        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loretto%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name traces back to a Jesuit mission in Canada and a Kentucky village where the Sisters of Loretto were founded in 1812.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loretto%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Loretto officially became a city in 1940, marking its transition from a rural settlement to an incorporated municipality.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loretto%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Located 19 miles west of Minneapolis, Loretto is an outer suburb entirely surrounded by the agricultural landscape of Medina.",
